  "answer_text": "Here is a summary of the latest news and developments regarding **Ukraine** as of May 31, 2026:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\uddfa\ud83c\udde6 Ukraine \u2014 Latest Developments\n\n### \u2694\ufe0f Military Situation\n\n- Russia's advance has suddenly stalled, and Ukraine is fighting on its own terms \u2014 a comeback credited to Kyiv's efforts to steadily strengthen the capabilities of its drones (UAVs).\n\n- Ukrainian Commander-in-Chief Oleksandr Syrskii stated that Ukraine has seized the tactical initiative, as Ukrainian offensive assaults on Russian positions now outnumber Russian assaults on Ukrainian positions.\n\n- General Oleksandr Komarenko claimed that Ukrainian forces restored control over 285.6 km\u00b2 in the Oleksandrivka direction and cleared 400 km\u00b2 of territory since the beginning of counteroffensive operations. February 2026 became the first month since 2024 when Ukraine regained more territory than it lost.\n\n- The village of Novoselivka in Dnipropetrovsk Oblast has reportedly been liberated from Russian occupation.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca5 Strikes & Attacks\n\n- Russian attacks killed 5 and injured 40 across Ukraine over the past day, including the destruction of a civilian train station in Sumy Oblast.\n\n- Ukraine has scaled up attacks on refineries across Russia, with Ukrainian drone attacks knocking out about 700,000 barrels per day (bpd) of refining capacity between January and May across 16 refineries.\n\n- A Russian brigade that committed war crimes in Bucha was hit by a Ukrainian drone strike, targeting the 64th Separate Motorized Rifle Brigade's training ground.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcca Casualties\n\n- Ukraine's General Staff reports Russia has lost 1,362,500 troops since February 24, 2022, including 1,430 casualties over the past day.\n\n- According to the UN human rights office (OHCHR), more civilians were killed or injured in Ukraine during the first four months of 2026 than during the same period in 2025, with 815 civilian deaths and 4,174 injuries verified between January and April.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf0d International Reaction\n\n- The United Nations warned of a dangerous escalation after a wave of large-scale Russian strikes on May 23\u201324, with Secretary-General Ant\u00f3nio Guterres saying the conflict risks spiralling \"out of control\" due to the dangers of miscalculation and \"unknown and unintended consequences.\"\n\n- President Zelensky met with top officials and announced preparations for \"important negotiations,\" with the agenda focused on acquiring more air defense interceptor missiles and joint drone production with the United States and European partners.\n\n- Japan purchased over $14 million in military equipment for Ukraine under a NATO weapons program, though Japan's contribution is limited to non-lethal aid.\n\n---\n\nThe situation remains extremely active, with intense fighting on multiple fronts, continued drone warfare, and growing international diplomatic pressure for a ceasefire. Would you like more details on any specific aspect?",
